  "result": "Perfect! All 129 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT (Value Added Tax) calculation to the invoice system:\n\n**Changes to `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n1. **`lineVAT(line)`** \u2014 Calculates VAT for a single line:\n   - Computes on the line amount **after discount**: `(line total - line discount) \u00d7 vatRate \u00f7 100`\n   - Each line's VAT is rounded individually to whole cents\n\n2. **Updated `invoiceTotals`** \u2014 Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`:\n   - `vat` = sum of all rounded line VATs\n   - `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0, never negative)\n\n**Changes to `src/render.js`:**\n\nUpdated `renderInvoiceText` to show VAT line just above the total:\n```\nINV-2026-0001\nCustomer Name\n5 \u00d7 Product @ \u20ac85.00 = \u20ac425.00\n...\nVAT: \u20ac89.25\nTotal: \u20ac514.25\n```\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- VAT calculated **per line** on amount after discount, not as a percentage of invoice total\n- Line VATs rounded individually, then summed\n- Products have vatRate of 0, 9, or 21 percent\n- All amounts shown to customers formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Tests added (14 new, 129 total):**\n- Line VAT calculation with various discounts\n- VAT with different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n- Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n- VAT interaction with discounts and tiers\n- Complex scenarios combining all features\n- Render output with VAT line\n- Zero-VAT products\n\nAll 129 tests pass. \u2705",
